# === Security hard rule: dev docs MUST NOT enter this repo ===
# Workspace policy (user-mandated, 2026-09-04):
#   All development / planning / review documents live in D:\job-learn
#   (a non-git working area). They MUST NOT be tracked here. The
#   patterns below are defensive: even if such a file is accidentally
#   copied into the tree, it will be silently excluded from tracking.
#   Never bypass with `git add -f` on these — a leak of pre-publication
#   security-review notes would telegraph unpatched vulnerabilities.

# Chinese planning / review / decomposition naming conventions
*规划*.md
*计划*.md
*审查*.md
*拆解*.md
*分析*.md
*复盘*.md
*草稿*.md

# Working / scratch directories
dev-notes/
scratch/
planning/
drafts/
notes/
working/

# Workbuddy memory + skills (workspace-level, not project source)
.workbuddy/

# Editor / OS temp + backup files
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Environment & secrets (never commit)
.env
.env.local

# Project docs (user-mandated: keep out of the GitHub repo)
docs/

# Editor/IDE + workspace assistant metadata
.idea/
.trae/

# Local state (checkpointer db)
*.db
*.sqlite3

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
